KokoroBox Desktop on Gentoo
==========================

Build provenance
----------------
This package compiles the main process, preload and React renderer from upstream
Desktop tag 3.26.9-5 using electron-vite. It never downloads or repacks a Desktop
release app.asar. It is not an entirely from-source software stack: Electron
44.3.0, Mihomo 1.19.30 and KokoroBox Service 0.2.4 are pinned upstream binaries in
the Manifest. The upstream pnpm lockfile supplies kokorobox-native 0.8.2, its N-API
module and its architecture-specific traffic presenter as prebuilt npm packages.
The bundled amd64 Mihomo and service require an x86-64-v3 CPU.

The ebuild bootstraps pnpm 11.1.1 from a Manifest-verified tarball and installs
JavaScript dependencies with --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts. The upstream
lockfile, dependency patch and workspace build settings are preserved, except
that supportedArchitectures is restricted to the build host to exclude foreign
native binaries. Upstream publishes no offline dependency bundle;
RESTRICT=network-sandbox permits this locked npm
installation to access the registry. This is deliberately not an offline build.
The npm package integrity hashes come from the upstream lockfile, not the Gentoo
Manifest. A complete pre-fetched npm bundle would be needed to remove this
restriction. Package lifecycle scripts and upstream prepare.ts are not run:
they otherwise download moving cores, geodata, fonts and a service prerelease.

The upstream system-core build mode instead uses the installed, pinned Mihomo
at /opt/kokorobox/resources/sidecar/mihomo and the pinned service at
/opt/kokorobox/resources/files/kokorobox-service. This mode disables bundled-core
switching/updating; there is no moving alpha core. It omits the downloaded emoji
font and bundled geodata. Profiles that use geodata require Mihomo to retrieve
those data at runtime (network access), or the user to supply them in their core
data directory. Normal proxy use does not require the privileged service.

Runtime and privileges
----------------------
Run kokorobox as your desktop user. Electron's sandbox is not disabled by the
launcher. Chromium's chrome-sandbox helper is root-owned and mode 4755, as
required by the bundled runtime. Neither core nor service is installed setuid,
and installation does not create or activate a service.

Use the app's permission/service panel to explicitly install and initialize
KokoroBox Service if privileged features such as TUN are needed. This invokes
the pinned service through pkexec and requires a running polkit authentication
agent and an init system supported by upstream's helper. Select service mode
and initialize the per-user service authentication before enabling TUN. Do not
run the whole Electron application as root or grant setuid to Mihomo. OpenRC
service integration is not supplied by this package; ordinary unprivileged
proxy operation remains available without it.

Use Portage for application/core/service updates, not the upstream updater.
Before removing this package, remove any service you explicitly registered
through the same permission/service panel; that registration is outside Portage.
The source and -bin packages conflict because both own /opt/kokorobox and the
kokorobox launcher. Existing user settings are not removed by either package.
